// Crossing-voice horizontal note-collision: the lower voice (voice 2, stem-down)
// crosses ABOVE the upper voice (voice 1, stem-up), so voice 1's stems would
// pierce voice 2's noteheads. LilyPond's note-collision "meshing" fallback nudges
// the crossed heads apart; voice 2's A5 quarters KEEP the column and voice 1's
// beamed C5 eighths move RIGHT to clear them. Mixed rhythm (8ths vs quarters)
// exercises one collision per quarter (at beats 1..4), each independently offset.
// LILYPOND-REF: lily/note-collision.cc:332-337 (meshing fallback).
// LILYPOND-REF: lily/note-collision.cc:441,462-463 left_most — the pin is the
//   LEFTMOST group, here the down one, and is not branched on collision type.
// MEASURED (LilyPond 2.26.0, twin of this book): the down head sits at x=17.1208
// and the up head at 17.5643; the same twin with the DOWN voice replaced by rests
// draws the lone up head at 17.1208 — the column the down voice keeps. This file
// used to state the opposite ("voice 2's A5 quarters shift LEFT"), which was
// Lily#'s inverted pin, itself a workaround for the beam frame not carrying the
// shift; both are gone (session 189).
octave absolute
title "Crossing-voice note collision"
part mel { clef treble }
section S {
  mel {
    voice { c'8 c' c' c' c' c' c' c' | }
    { a'4 a' a' a' | }
  }
}
form main { S }
score main "multivoice-crossing-collision" { staff mel }
